019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,641,4149,27665,285,11,458,6683,374,264,1697,220,17,16,1635,315,4231,476,9014,323,264,1682,374,264,1697,1212,220,17,16,1635,315,4231,13,220,68490,4279,315,279,220,12598,304,4149,27665,285,525,8778,11,323,6896,4279,315,279,8778,220,12598,614,6896,825,23275,1682,13,220,36458,770,702,264,220,1682,11,323,1052,525,902,1008,2841,13,220,3555,3266,315,279,220,1251,315,4149,27665,285,525,2841,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn Mathopolis, an adult is a person 21 years of age or older and a child is a person under 21 years of age.  Exactly half of the  adults in Mathopolis are female, and exactly half of the female  adults have exactly one biological child.  Nobody else has a  child, and there are no other children.  What percent of the  people of Mathopolis are children?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"1317299447347b27086dbdb21b90cf1d78f9b55fa3895c09c4af047d62d7497d"},"seconds":9.579862356185913,"seed":306381167922435726,"stop":"eos","text":"Let's denote the total number of adults in Mathopolis as \\( A \\). According to the problem, exactly half of the adults are female, so the number of female adults is \\( \\frac{A}{2} \\).\n\nWe are also given that exactly half of the female adults have exactly one biological child. Therefore, the number of female adults who have one child each is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{A}{2} = \\frac{A}{4} \\). Since these are the only children in Mathopolis, the total number of children is \\( \\frac{A}{4} \\).\n\nNext, we need to determine the total population of Mathopolis. The population consists of both adults and children. Since the number of children is \\( \\frac{A}{4} \\), the total population \\( P \\) is the sum of the number of adults and the number of children:\n\\[ P = A + \\frac{A}{4} = \\frac{4A}{4} + \\frac{A}{4} = \\frac{5A}{4} \\]\n\nWe are asked to find the percentage of the population that consists of children. The number of children is \\( \\frac{A}{4} \\), so the percentage of the population that consists of children is:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{\\frac{A}{4}}{\\frac{5A}{4}} \\right) \\times 100 = \\left( \\frac{A}{4} \\times \\frac{4}{5A} \\right) \\times 100 = \\left( \\frac{1}{5} \\right) \\times 100 = 20\\% \\]\n\nThus, the percentage of the people of Mathopolis who are children is \\(\\boxed{20}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{20}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:385"}
